    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 34 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule following this codebase's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern. The tier is derived at read time in `OwnerMapper` from persisted fields on `Owner` (the same design used for the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules via `namesakeCount`), so I added a persisted household-size count populated during the create pipeline.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdMemberCount` field (`household_member_count` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_member_count` column to the `owners` table.\n\n3. **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** (new pipeline step) \u2014 after `AssignHousehold` has assigned/back-filled the shared `householdId`, it counts owners sharing that id (existing members in the repo + this not-yet-saved owner) and stores the total. A lone owner with no `householdId` gets a household of 1.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignHouseholdSize` step between `assignHousehold` and `countNamesakes`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now returns `GOLD` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, otherwise falls back to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document GOLD (the field is a free-form string, so no enum change was needed).\n\nThe new `Cp23Tests` (GOLD for a 3-member household) and the existing `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE) both pass, along with the entire acceptance suite.",
